  "notes": "Eastern Min (Mìng-dĕ̤ng-ngṳ̄ / Mindong), Fuzhou dialect, romanised input contract: Bàng-uâ-cê (Foochow Romanized, Maclay & Baldwin 1870). e̤/o̤ spell mid-central/back vowels distinct from e/o, each earning its key by test 2 (one vowel quality per spelling, blocked from collapsing onto the plain-letter grapheme). ng is the velar-nasal onset/coda (test 2). Tone is lexical (7 citation tones plus sandhi) and not yet encoded; the stress schema does not apply, tonal-language exemption per quality_tiers.md. No WikiPron gold exists in this romanisation (WikiPron's cdo_hani file is Han-character keyed), so the tier stays at skeleton.",
